---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Collections" description="Collections of notes, themes, and longer-form reflections.">
  <header class="page-header shell split-header">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">COLLECTIONS</p><h1>Themed note<br /><em>collections.</em></h1></div>
    <p>Longer-form threads and curated sets of entries that illuminate repeating patterns and ideas.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="case-study shell" id="rough-at-sea">
    <div class="case-study-index">CASE 001</div>
    <div class="case-study-main">
      <div class="case-study-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">PERSONAL NOTEBOOK</p><h2>Rough at Sea</h2></div>
        <p class="case-study-year">2026</p>
      </div>

      <div class="case-study-hero">
        <div class="case-radar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>R/S</span></div>
        <div class="case-caption"><span>FROM PLATFORM</span><strong>TO NOTEBOOK</strong></div>
      </div>

      <div class="case-study-story">
        <div><p class="section-number">THE SITUATION</p><h3>A capable system for a problem that no longer needed one.</h3></div>
        <p>The earlier site was heavier; over time the notebook's needs shifted: the content mattered more than the machinery.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="decision-grid">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Keep the notes accessible</h3><p>Entries live as Markdown files and render statically so the book remains easy to read and move between platforms.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>Let the ideas breathe</h3><p>Present content in a calm, reflective layout that emphasizes the note over the platform.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Make the structure familiar</h3><p>The interface is built to feel like a notebook: clear headings, simple categories, and gentle visual signals.</p></article>
      </div>

      <div class="outcome-strip">
        <div><strong>0</strong><span>external services</span></div>
        <div><strong>0</strong><span>sign-in flows</span></div>
        <div><strong>1</strong><span>interactive experiment</span></div>
        <div><strong>100%</strong><span>readable pages</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
